Explanation}
\par \pard\plain \s67\loch\ql\widctlpar\sb180\sa180\ltrpar{\loch
Disciple needs a bit of a general rework. His class is Soldier, and while I understand why Obsidian made it that way and have decided to keep it, a typical soldier\u8217\'92s statline doesn\u8217\'92t really fit what he does as a pseudo-spy/historian. He\u8217\'92s Jedi-trained but that was years in the past; he\u8217\'92s a well-educated, erudite student at this point, not Buff McLargehuge as his vanilla statline implies.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\loch\ql\widctlpar\sb180\sa180\ltrpar{\loch
One feat he shouldn\u8217\'92t have had for his level has been removed, and his feats have also been reshuffled somewhat: he loses Improved Toughness down to regular Toughness, to represent the years since he\u8217\'92s been Jedi-trained, and in return granted him Empathy\u8212\'97this is a thematic mod, after all, and even though it\u8217\'92s far from optimal the Disciple\u8217\'92s intense and consistent empathy for the Jedi is a major plot point. He additionally loses Close Combat in exchange for Finesse: Melee, to make his higher DEX a bit more inherently viable.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\loch\ql\widctlpar\sb180\sa180\ltrpar{\loch
His attributes were also reworked to reflect his erudition and intuition, which even Kreia praises (when she doesn\u8217\'92t uncritically praise anyone else but the Exile in the entire game!). Some of his physical capabilities remain, because he\u8217\'92s clearly a field agent, but he\u8217\'92s no longer presented as a himbo. He\u8217\'92s got training, but his most fertile field is the mind, not the body.}
