Explanation}
\par \pard\plain \s67\loch\ql\widctlpar\sb180\sa180\ltrpar{\loch
Wow Hanharr, why do you have vanilla Zaalbar\u8217\'92s attribute line?}
\par \pard\plain \s63\loch\ql\widctlpar\sb180\sa180\ltrpar{\loch
Even though it\u8217\'92s just ripped from K1, Hanharr has a very inflated statline for his level, but it isn\u8217\'92t quite so simple as that. Part of that needs to be understood as compensation for not receiving Mira, who can be made a Jedi; part is compensation for not being able to equip body armor; and part is because Wookiees don\u8217\'92t have normal human physical limitations.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\loch\ql\widctlpar\sb180\sa180\ltrpar{\loch
The balance on this was difficult to do in a thematically consistent way, but I set a baseline rationale that Wookiees would most logically have a +2 STR/+2 CON racial bonus, and the \u8220\'93price\u8221\'94 for that was the inability to wear armor in exchange. Proceeding from that baseline assumption, Hanharr\u8217\'92s STR and CON have been reduced from 20 to 18 in both cases, which now leaves him at a normal starting attribute line (plus the +1 attribute selection at level 4, which he starts at) when factoring in the assumed +2 STR/+2 CON racial bonus. His skills are also slightly reshuffled, primarily to give him the stealth he must\u8217\'92ve had as a shadowlands hunter.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\loch\ql\widctlpar\sb180\sa180\ltrpar{\loch
He has lost Close Combat and gained Toughness both because I believe this better fits his character (Hanharr is never shown to use ranged weapons, after all) and because otherwise he would come at level 4 with two feats that could only be selected at level 4 (Improved Power Attack and Close Combat). This way he starts with only feats he could have actually selected at his level.}
