\par \pard\plain \s67\loch\ql\widctlpar\sb180\sa180\ltrpar{\loch
Oh wow look it\u8217\'92s Bastila\u8217\'92s statline, how quaint.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\loch\ql\widctlpar\sb180\sa180\ltrpar{\loch
In honesty, Bastila\u8217\'92s attributes fit Visas fairly well, and I have mostly kept them, save for removing some of her DEX to make her attributes actually match what they should be at her level. The main thing that needed to be done for Visas was a cleanup of her feats, powers and base stats. She has two more feats than she should, one less power than she should, and a LOT less base vitality/Force than she should.}
\par \pard\plain \s63\loch\ql\widctlpar\sb180\sa180\ltrpar{\loch
I suspect the lack of base Force is meant to represent Nihilus\u8217\'92s predations upon her, and ditto the Vitality. I can understand this reasoning, but Visas is already the only Jedi companion in the entire game which doesn\u8217\'92t receive Force Sensitivity, and that already knocks 40 possible Force points off of her total; she doesn\u8217\'92t need to be savaged harder. Similarly, while I understand the reduced Vitality from the physical and indeed metaphysical trauma she\u8217\'92s suffered, I think that\u8217\'92s best represented with the CON reduction I gave her rather than with an arbitrary off-the-top reduction of her base vitality. This way her vitality is still reduced some, but it\u8217\'92s in a more usable range, and investments in her CON can represent her healing\u8212\'97both physical and mental\u8212\'97during her journey.}
